From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:35:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: learn the resistance
 against the start-up OCV

The resistance is learned only within 24 hours of an OCV reading taken
at rest, so that the estimate does not rest on a reading that itself
depends on the resistance. The start-up OCV, sampled by the PMIC before
the load, was not counted as such, so a boot that began from it learned
nothing until a rest or a finished charge: on one boot an all-core load
at 1.5-1.8 A ran for five minutes with the headroom on its aged-cell
assumption, while the samples showed about 0.4 Ohm.

Count the start-up OCV as a rested reading for learning the resistance.
It does not depend on the resistance; surface charge after a charge
would only make the estimate a little high, the safe side for the
headroom.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index 867d68b..3bfcb23 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -1018,7 +1018,12 @@ static void mt6351_fg_pwron_anchor(struct mt6351_fg *fg)
 	fg->anchor_uah = div_s64(fg->full_uah * clamp(pct, 0, 100), 100);
 	fg->anchor_car = fg->car;
 	fg->anchor_time = ktime_get_boottime();
-	fg->anchor_trusted = false;
+	/*
+	 * Taken before the load, it does not depend on the resistance, so the
+	 * resistance can be learned against it; surface charge would only make
+	 * the estimate a little high, the safe side.
+	 */
+	fg->anchor_trusted = true;
 	fg->anchored = true;
 	dev_info(fg->dev, "start-up OCV %d uV: %d %% of the OCV table\n", uv, pct);
 }
